      "text": "Forming Coherent Belief Systems\n\nFigure 1.2\nTwo cognitive pathways in worldview formation: Passive and Reflective\n\n                             INPUTS\n                      (Culture, upbringing, education, media, peer norms,\n                                           authority)\n\n       From Passive Worldview Adoption     To Reflective Worldview Adoption\n\n           AUTOMATIC              METACOGNITIVE\n          INTERPRETATION              AWARENESS\n                     (This feels                       (This is an intuition, not a\n            normal/obvious/reasonable)                     conclusion)\n\n           COGNITIVE BIAS                DELIBERATE\n          REINFORCEMENT              EVALUATION\n             (Confirmation bias, social                  (logical consistency, evidence\n             proof, availability, identity                comparison, explanatory\n                     protection)                             power)\n\n           WORLDVIEW            REASONED WORLDVIEW\n             FIXATION               COMMITMENT\n            (Resistance to disconfirming              (Best conclusion from available\n                     evidence)                                 evidence)\n\n         No desire to engage in            Shows intellectual humility. Open\n                effortful reasoning.                 to revision as evidence improves.\n\n                                 6",
      "source_kind": "authored_research",
      "evidence_role": "argument_not_scripture",
