      "text": "33 A quire is simply a small booklet made of folded parchment sheets before binding.\n34 Michael Marx, “Topkapı Palace Museum: Saray Medina 1a,” Corpus Coranicum,\nmanuscript catalogue; Haytham Sidky, \"On the Regionality of Qurʾānic Codices,\" Journal of\nthe International Qur’anic Studies Association (JIQSA) 5 (2020): 133–210 (specifically pp.\n148–156); Marijn van Putten, “‘The Grace of God’ as Evidence for a Written Uthmanic\nArchetype: The Importance of Shared Orthographic Idiosyncrasies,” Bulletin of the School\nof Oriental and African Studies 82, no. 2 (2019): 271–288.\n35 Morteza Karimi-Nia, \"A New Document in the Early History of the Qurʾān: Codex\nMashhad, an Ibn Masʿūd Text-Type?\" Journal of Islamic Manuscripts 10, no. 3 (2019): 292–\n326).\n                                56",
