      "text": "68 Gustave Le Bon, The Crowd: A Study of the Popular Mind; Jacques Ellul, Propaganda:\nThe Formation of Men’s Attitudes; Stanley Milgram, Obedience to Authority; Solomon E.\nAsch, “Opinions and Social Pressure.”\n69 Aktharuhum la yu’minoon — Most of them do not believe — (2:100; 11:17; 13:1; 40:59);\n Akthara nasi la yashkuroon — Most of the people are ungrateful — (2:243; 7:17; 10:60;\n12:38; 27:73; 40:61); Aktharuhum ul Fasiqoon — Most of them are wicked — (3:110; 5:59;\n7:102; 9:8); Aktharuhum la Ya’qiloon — Most of them do not reason — (5:103; 25:44;\n29:63; 49:4); Aktharuhum la Ya’lamoon — Most of them do not know — (6:37; 7:131;\n7:187; 8:34; 10:55; 12:21; 12:40; 12:68; 16:38; 16:75; 16:101; 21:24; 27:61; 28:13; 28:57;\n30:6; 30:30; 31:25; 34:28; 34:36; 39:29; 39:49; 40:57; 44:39; 45:26; 52:47); Aktharuhum\nYajahiloon — Most of them are ignorant — (6:111); Aktharuhum ul Kafiroon — Most of\nthem are rejecters — (16:83; 17:89; 25:50); Wa ma kana Aktharuhum momineen — Most\nof them are not believers — (12:103; 26:8; 26:67; 26:103; 26:121; 26:139; 26:158; 26:174;\n26:190; 34:41); Aktharuhum Kaziboon — Most of them are liars — (26:223); Aktharuhum\nlil’haqqi karihoon — Most are averse to truth — (23:70; 43:78); Aktharuhum Mushrikeen\n                                100",
