      "text": "The Seven Domains of Qurʾānic Philosophy\n\nTable 6.2\nSummarized view of the seven philosophical domains\n\n                    Key\n                                 Divine Act /    Philosophical #      Phase       Qurʾānic                                         Function\n                            Theme       Domain\n                       Verses\n\n 1   Ontological   Q 32:7-9;    Formation      Ontology /       Existence and awareness\n     Formation      15:28-29     from clay;        Consciousness   (What am I?)\n                                     infusion of rūḥ\n\n 2   Semantic    Q 2:31–33   Teaching of      Epistemology /   Meaning, language,\n     Induction                  names           Logic             reasoning, differentiation\n                                                   (How do I know?)\n\n 3   Moral      Q 30:30;     Imprint of       Axiology /       Innate moral orientation\n      Calibration      91:8; 7:172   fiṭrah           Value         (Why do I incline toward\n                                                                      the good?)\n\n 4   Free       Q 33:72      Bestowal of      Praxeology /     Freedom and\n      Responsibility            amānah          Ethics            accountability (How\n                                                                   should I act?)\n\n 5   Purpose of   Q 21:35;     Creation as test   Teleology /       Life as the arena of moral\n      Life            67:2          (fitnah /         Purpose           testing (What is my\n                                            ibtilāʾ)                           purpose?)",
