      "text": "Reason, Revelation and the Architecture of Truth\n   The most powerful modern example is artificial neural networks that cannot\nfunction without:\n    •   architecture/equations (deduction),\n    •   training data (induction),\n    •   loss function optimization (abduction).\n   The system cannot move a single step without reasoning logic embedded in the\ncode. There is no emergence without the triad.\n\nGenetic Algorithms (GAs)89\n    Popularly claimed to mimic evolution, they succeed only because the “proxy\ncreator” decides how the overall design will look, and once those rules have been pre-\ndecided, writes code to run the simulation. A loss function is used to inform on what\ncounts as “better,” selection pressure is intentionally engineered, and allowable\nmutations are artificially constrained. While GAs are assumed to be stochastic\noptimization tools, they use a pseudo-random number generator (PRNG) that is\ninherently deterministic and needs an initial seed. The problem remains confined to\na defined search space.\n\nTable 7.3\nThe five functional elements of a GA mapped to the three reasoning modes.\n     GA Step          Reasoning                Conceptual Connection\n                     Mode\n Representation &                      Sampling the solution space through exposure to varied\n                         Induction\n  initialization                              candidates\n\n                                      Each candidate is judged through fixed logical rules  Fitness evaluation        Deduction\n                                           defined by the objective function\n                                      Choosing best-performing hypotheses as likely solution\n  Selection operator       Abduction\n                                             direction",
