      "text": "95 David Hume argued that what we call “necessity” is not an observable force binding events\nin the world, but a psychological expectation formed by repeated experience. When one\nevent regularly follows another, the mind comes to feel that the second must follow the first\n— even though this necessity is never directly observed.\n                                169",
