      "text": "Appendix D: Early Qurʾānic Manuscripts\n\nThis table summarizes representative early Qurʾānic manuscripts across different regions, dates, and\npreservation states. Coverage percentages reflect surviving material, not original manuscript\ncompleteness. Textual characteristics describe correspondence at the consonantal (rasm) level unless\notherwise noted.\n\n                 Approx. Date    Preservation    Textual               Geographic\n   Manuscript\n                 (CE)           Coverage       Characteristics         Location\n\n   Codex          Probably 7th    >90%          Very High             Mashhad, Iran\n   Mashhad        century;                        Concordance:\n    (Ḥijāzī)        parchment                      Standard ʿUthmānic\n               C14 660–772                     rasm; originally\n              CE                              arranged in an\n                                                            alternative surah order\n                                                                 later modified.\n\n    Ṣanʿāʾ           7th – early 8th    Fragmentary    High Concordance:       Ṣanʿāʾ, Yemen\n    Palimpsest —    century           (multiple      Conforms almost        (Arabian\n   Upper Text                         sūrahs, partial   exactly to the standard    Peninsula)\n    (Standard                            verses)          Qurʾānic rasm.\n    Ḥijāzī)\n\n    Ṣanʿāʾ 1        Parchment       Fragmentary    Textually divergent:       Ṣanʿāʾ, Yemen\n   Palimpsest—    dated 578-669                 Non-ʿUthmānic textual\n   Lower Text    CE                              type with genuine\n    (Archaic                                     wording differences\n    Ḥijāzī)                                      and alternative surah\n                                                          order. Semantically\n                                                       non-divergent.",
