      "text": "59 Say thou: “O doctors of the Law: do you resent us save \nthat we believe in God and what was sent down to us and \nwhat was sent down before, and that most of you are \nperfidious?”\n60 Say thou: “Shall I inform you of worse than that as a \nrecompense with God? He whom God cursed and with \nwhom He was wroth and made of them apes and swine \nand servants of idols: those are worse in standing and \nfurther astray from the right path.”\n61 And when they come to you, they say: “We believe”; \nbut they entered in denial, and they left in it; and God best \nknows what they were concealing.\n62 And thou seest many of them competing in sin and \nenmity and their consumption of illicit gain; evil is what \nthey do.\n63 Oh, that the rabbis and the religious scholars had but\n\n2\t\nQur’anic verses not in italics are from The Qur’an: A Complete \nRevelation.",
