      "text": "f men in \nvanity, and turn away from the path of God. And those who \namass gold and silver and spend it not in the cause of God: \ngive thou them tidings of a painful punishment: —\n35 The day it will be heated in the fire of Gehenna, then \ntherewith will be branded their foreheads and their sides \nand their backs: “This is what you amassed for your souls; \nso taste what you amassed!”\n(9:29-35)\n\nThe topic in all cases is the responsibility of the ruling religious \nelite to implement the revelations they have from God and not to \nsell them ‘for a cheap price’ — a term which consistently treats \nof trading revelation for material gain — (2:41, 2:79, 2:174, \n3:77, 3:187, 3:199, 5:44, 9:9, 16:95); the failure of that religious \nelite to implement the same (5:59-5:66) — again in a material \nregard; the responsibility of the believers to fight those among",
