      "topics": [],
      "text": "3:135, 4:15, 4:19, 4:22, 4:25, 6:151, 7:28, 7:33, 7:80, 17:32, \n24:19, 27:54, 29:28, 33:30, 42:37, 53:32, 65:1.\n\nfaḥshā — sexual immorality\n\n2:169, 2:268, 7:28, 12:24, 16:90, 24:21, 29:45.\n\n32 And approach not unlawful sexual intercourse — it is \nsexual immorality, and evil as a path — \n(17:32)\n\n22 And marry not what your fathers married among \nwomen save what is past; it was sexual immorality, and \nhateful, and an evil path.\n(4:22)",
      "source_kind": "attributed_external_research",
      "evidence_role": "argument_not_scripture",
