      "topics": [],
      "text": "And O my people: how is it that I invite you to deliverance, and you invite \nme to the Fire? You call me to deny God, and to ascribe a partnership to Him \nwith that whereof I have no knowledge; and I invite you to the Exalted in \nMight, the Forgiver. Without doubt, you but invite me to that to which there \nis no calling in the World or in the Hereafter; and our return is to God. And \nthe committers of excess will be the companions of the Fire. And you will \nremember what I say to you. And I commit my affair to God; God sees the \nservants.\n\nThe Qur’an: A Complete Revelation, from 40:29-44",
      "source_kind": "third_party_book",
      "evidence_role": "argument_not_scripture",
      "external_discussion": false,
      "pdf_page": 5
