      "text": "12 Consider for example, 1:5, 72:20. One would do well to remember that Pharaoh is not interested in religion in the \nsense one is accustomed to think of that term today. He is interested in where a man’s primary loyalty lies: with him, or \nwith one other than him. The same dynamic is implicit in the elite-owned system of today: one either bows to the idol of \nGovernment or one does not.\n\n13 See for example 10:15.",
