      "text": "NON-CORE ACTIONS\n\nStates that his task is to convey message.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nCites previously destroyed peoples.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nAppeals to his people to wait as he is waiting.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nChallenges the unbelievers to do their worst.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nStresses the message given by God.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nResponds to derision or accusation.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nStates that destruction is the decision of God alone.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nAddresses subject of those who follow him.\nEXP\nEXP\n\nStates that he seeks no reward from those to whom he is \nconveying warning.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nPresents a proof.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nAccuses the hearers of invention of falsity.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nCites the favours of God.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nStates that he is a warner or messenger.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nExhorts the hearers to obey him.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nPresents a punishment which is contingent on response by \nhearers.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nUses the appeal: “O my people:”.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\n\nPlaces his affair entirely in the hands of God.\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nBears glad tidings and warning.\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nPresents a clear notification.\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nStates that God only can provide the authority requested.\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nStates that he is nothing more than a mortal.\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nAdvances reasoned arguments.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nAnticipates (punishment of) a “tremendous day”.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nWarns of punishment.\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\n\nAppeals to God.\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nEXP\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS\nGNS",
